/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 05\072 All members\073 either House\073 legislators\056 \215Legislators\216 means members of these law\055making institutions\056 Paragraph \05014\051 covers MPs\054 members of the House of Lords\054 MSPs\054 Members of the Senedd and MLAs\056 It includes peers who are not elected\056 It adds the members to the relevant definition\073 the legislatures themselves remain excluded as public authorities\056)
/Dest [ 30 0 R /FitR 38 506.9898 295.6378 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 93.51689 631.0298 157.7946 645.1898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 04\072 The UK\220s four legislatures\056 These are the UK Parliament in London\054 the Scottish Parliament in Edinburgh\054 Senedd Cymru in Cardiff\054 and the Northern Ireland Assembly in Belfast\056 A legislature debates and makes laws\056 The UK Parliament has two Houses\072 the House of Commons and the House of Lords\056 Together they are one legislature\056)
/Dest [ 18 0 R /FitR 299.6378 217.4898 557.2756 435.8898 ]
/Rect [ 220.9027 631.0298 305.0296 645.1898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 06\072 Duty of candour\056 Candour means being open\054 honest and frank\056 Clause 2 sets the duty of candour and assistance in dealings with the inquiries and investigations covered by the Bill\056 It includes notifying relevant information\054 providing assistance and correcting errors\054 subject to the Bill\220s rules\056 Clause 5 creates the offence for certain failures to comply\056)
/Dest [ 30 0 R /FitR 299.6378 522.4898 557.2756 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 363.73 631.0298 446.1053 645.1898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 08\072 Section 12\072 misleading the public\056 An incorrect statement alone is not enough\056 Section 12 requires intention or recklessness about misleading the public\054 significant or repeated dishonesty on a matter of significant public concern\054 actual or potential harm from the act\054 and a significant departure from proper functions\056 The person must know\054 or ought to know\054 that the act is seriously improper\073 a reasonable person must also consider it so in all the circumstances\056 The Bill\220s defences remain\056)
/Dest [ 30 0 R /FitR 299.6378 172.7898 557.2756 435.8898 ]
/Rect [ 490.9775 631.0298 541.7844 645.1898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 08\072 Section 12\072 misleading the public\056 An incorrect statement alone is not enough\056 Section 12 requires intention or recklessness about misleading the public\054 significant or repeated dishonesty on a matter of significant public concern\054 actual or potential harm from the act\054 and a significant departure from proper functions\056 The person must know\054 or ought to know\054 that the act is seriously improper\073 a reasonable person must also consider it so in all the circumstances\056 The Bill\220s defences remain\056)
/Dest [ 30 0 R /FitR 299.6378 172.7898 557.2756 435.8898 ]
/Rect [ 46 614.2298 157.835 628.3898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
155 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 09\072 Freedom of political expression and debate\056 This preserves room for political argument\054 criticism and disagreement\056 An unpopular policy or strongly expressed view does not become a crime simply because others object\056 Paragraph \05015\051 expressly protects honest mistakes and honestly held political opinions\054 alongside the existing freedom\055of\055expression right\056 The requirements of the relevant offence still have to be established\056)
/Dest [ 58 0 R /FitR 38 492.0898 295.6378 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 224.2676 614.2298 444.855 628.3898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
156 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 10\072 Parliamentary privilege and proceedings\056 At Westminster\054 Article IX of the Bill of Rights protects parliamentary speech\054 debates and proceedings from being questioned in court\056 This amendment expressly excludes sections 5 and 12 for proceedings in all four legislatures\056 That includes formal parliamentary work\054 such as debates and committee evidence\073 it does not cover everything said anywhere in a Parliament building\056)
/Dest [ 58 0 R /FitR 299.6378 492.0898 557.2756 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 450.8875 614.2298 524.9198 628.3898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 10\072 Parliamentary privilege and proceedings\056 At Westminster\054 Article IX of the Bill of Rights protects parliamentary speech\054 debates and proceedings from being questioned in court\056 This amendment expressly excludes sections 5 and 12 for proceedings in all four legislatures\056 That includes formal parliamentary work\054 such as debates and committee evidence\073 it does not cover everything said anywhere in a Parliament building\056)
/Dest [ 58 0 R /FitR 299.6378 492.0898 557.2756 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 46 597.4298 91.13154 611.5898 ]
