/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 11\072 Honest mistakes\056 A person does not commit either offence merely by making a genuine mistake\056 Being wrong is different from being dishonest\056 This protection does not excuse separate conduct that satisfies the offence\054 such as deliberately concealing a known correction\056 The word \215merely\216 keeps that distinction clear\056)
/Dest [ 58 0 R /FitR 38 217.4898 295.6378 435.8898 ]
/Rect [ 119.7039 597.4298 203.7155 611.5898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 17\072 Democratic voice as a public function\056 This names the central idea\072 addressing the public about matters of significant public concern forms part of the official role of the listed legislators\054 ministers and mayors\056 \215Democratic\216 describes their role in democratic institutions\073 it does not mean every office\055holder is elected\056 Paragraph \05016\051 gives this idea its specific legal effect for this Bill\056)
/Dest [ 79 0 R /FitR 38 523.1898 295.6378 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 326.7167 597.4298 414.5656 611.5898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
