161 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 21\072 Government Ministers\056 These include UK ministers and ministers in the Scottish\054 Welsh and Northern Ireland governments\056 Ministers are already covered through the Bill\220s existing definitions\056 Paragraph \05016\051 names their legal categories so its public\055communications rule applies to them too\054 including relevant junior ministers and law officers\056)
/Dest [ 88 0 R /FitR 38 522.4898 295.6378 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 46 580.6298 163.9078 594.7898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 23\072 Which mayors are included\077\056 Here \215mayors\216 means the Mayor of London and mayors for the areas of combined authorities or combined county authorities\056 These offices are already covered by the Bill\056 Paragraph \05016\051 expressly applies the public\055communications rule to them\056 It does not add every local council mayor\054 councillor or police and crime commissioner to that rule\056)
/Dest [ 88 0 R /FitR 38 202.5898 295.6378 435.8898 ]
/Rect [ 189.2939 580.6298 227.7419 594.7898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Border [ 0 0 0 ]
/Contents (Note 18\072 Public functions\056 These are the duties and activities belonging to someone\220s public role\056 The Bill limits public\055official status to those functions\056 Paragraph \05016\051 expressly makes the listed people\220s public communications on matters of significant public concern count as exercising public functions\054 subject to its judicial and purely private exclusions\056)
/Dest [ 79 0 R /FitR 299.6378 522.4898 557.2756 740.8898 ]
/Rect [ 309.7484 580.6298 393.835 594.7898 ]
/Subtype /Link
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
